From 3f94f1ca6683c68f7e5655a689192b22fb4f5b8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:01:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: profile 5 pixels drawn over converted in a
 pass of their own

Where decoding is not affine (IPT-PQ-c2, profile 5), converting a pixel drawn over back to codes
takes three PQ round trips, and the pass of the transport converted each pixel twice: for its own
luma, and for the chroma of its pair, which an odd pixel takes from the even one, so the odd pixel
converted the even one again. Under a GUI that spans most of the raster (the background of the
player information spans its width and three quarters of its height) the packing of a frame took
60 ms on the integrated Radeon of a Ryzen 9 7950X3D through D3D12, five times what it takes for
profiles 7 and 8.1. On that GPU with radeonsi, a profile 5 film took 43 to 54 ms of GPU time a
frame of the 41.7 ms of a 24 Hz refresh with the player information open, and 10.6 ms without it,
in a test of the build before.

A pass before the transport (pass 8) now converts the pixels drawn over, a fragment for each pair
of the raster in the tiles that the GUI may reach (or over the whole raster where that is not
known), into a texture of codes: drawn_over() of the even pixel for its luma, another call of it
for the chroma, and one of the odd pixel for its luma, three calls where the transport made four.
The transport takes their codes. The two calls of the even pixel are kept apart, as the transport
had them: one call for both, or for parts of both, gave the same codes on lavapipe and on an RTX
4080 SUPER, but not on the integrated Radeon through D3D12, where the chroma came out a code apart
on about one pixel drawn over in 20,000, at values within 0.03 of a half. drawn_over(), to_source()
and code() moved, unchanged, into DRAWN_OVER, which both passes take. The affine profiles do not
take the pass. Where it cannot be made, the transport converts the pixels itself as before: the
same codes, more slowly.

Measured with a host test of the bridge (162 frames of profile 5, 7 FEL and 8.1 pictures with
Kodi's GUI composited over them, as for the commit before): the same bytes as before on lavapipe
and on the integrated Radeon and the RTX 4080 SUPER through D3D12; seven mutations of the pass made
them differ, and without the pass they stay the same. On the integrated Radeon, a profile 5 frame
under the player information takes 58.9 ms (76.7 ms after the commit before, 83.1 ms before it), a
window over a dimmed screen 70.7 ms (93.0, 101.9), the OSD 29.8 ms (35.2, 37.6); profiles 7 FEL and
8.1 stay as they were, and on the RTX 4080 SUPER every frame takes under 3.5 ms either way.
Radeonsi, the driver of that GPU in LibreELEC, is not verified.
